Z||000000||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-11-2001||03:30 PM||||Anyone know if any other cars share the strut top (strut assembly?) with any other  cars? (same 3 bolt holes?)<P>I might go look at the wreckers for a set for my 84', but they have no fieros..<P><BR>TIA!<P><BR>||||reg||1
Z||000001||isthiswhereiputausername?||10-11-2001||06:02 PM||||anyone? <P>||||reg||1
Z||000002||theogre||10-11-2001||06:59 PM||||The plate that the strut is actually bolted into is not the same as FWD cars. FWD cars all use a full bearing assembly that allows the spring to rotate as you steer the car. The Fiero doen't need and won't likely accept such a setup.<P>It is still available thru regular autoparts channels but will need to be ordered. Moog and others list it...<P>------------------<BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/fullstaff.gif">   <FONT COLOR="blue"><I><B>11-Sept-01, The day the world as we knew it ended.</B></I></FONT><p>[This message has been edited by theogre (edited 10-11-2001).]||||reg||1
